  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the peninsula linking the Pins cove and the Tabarly cove, in the Mourillon area, the "dog beach" is Toulon's first dog beach (the city calls Pipady the "second" after it). A pontoon makes it easier to get into the water and swim. Residents have however pointed out that water access there suits small dogs or non-swimmers less well (Toulon Magazine no. 3, RCF Méditerranée, July 2026).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the municipal order of 28 September 2026, this area is dedicated to dogs year-round; the city publishes neither hours nor fees. The nearby Mourillon beaches remain closed to dogs on the sand and lawns (Henri-Fabre promenade allowed on a leash); human swimming is prohibited by the Tabarly cove.</p>
      <p>Something to note for the future: according to Toulon's mayor (Toulon Magazine no. 1, April 2026, then a toulon.fr article of 31 July 2026), the Pipady dog beach, opened on 1 July 2026, is eventually to replace the Tabarly cove one, "destined to disappear" with the redevelopment works of the nautical base. The order of 28 September 2026 still mentions it: no closing date is known, so check if you plan to come regularly.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the city publishes no hours for this area, but it is due to close eventually; the nearby Pipady dog beach is the alternative to favour if in doubt.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Mourillon beaches and the Henri-Fabre promenade are in the same area, as is the <a href="/en/fiche-pipady-toulon">Pipady dog beach</a>, at the foot of the Tour Royale.</p>
    </div>

